Texere is released under two licenses, depending on the type of content.

1. Code: MIT License
   Applies to: Support/Admin/Scripts/, Support/Templates/New laptop setup.md and the
   Texere plugins in .obsidian/plugins/texere/, .obsidian/plugins/texere-sources/ and
   .obsidian/plugins/texere-export/ (except the bundled third-party files listed below).

2. Guides and notes: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   Applies to: the guides and notes in Support/About/ and Support/Guides/, the philosophy map
   in Fields/, the templates in Support/Templates/ and the example notes in
   01. Sources/Literature Notes/.
   Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
   You may share and adapt this material for any purpose, as long as you give
   appropriate credit to George Mihai (https://www.georgemihai.com) and indicate if
   changes were made.

Not covered by these licenses:
   - The PDFs and other files in 01. Sources/Documents/, which belong to their
     respective authors and publishers.
   - The community plugins in .obsidian/plugins/ (other than texere, texere-sources and
     texere-export), which are distributed under their own licenses by their authors.
   - .obsidian/plugins/texere-sources/sources/citeproc.js (citeproc-js by Frank Bennett,
     CPAL 1.0 or AGPL 3.0).
   - The citation styles (Support/Admin/Bibliography/*.csl), the CSL locales
     (.obsidian/plugins/texere-sources/sources/locales/) and the style list
     (.obsidian/plugins/texere-sources/sources/styles-index.json), distributed under
     CC BY-SA 3.0 by the Citation Style Language project.
   - The libraries bundled in .obsidian/plugins/texere-export/: lib-docx.js (docx by
     Dolan Miu), lib-markdown.js (markdown-it and markdown-it-footnote) and lib-paged.js
     (Paged.js), each under the MIT License by its authors.

